{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And repays His enemies.</b> To each one of His enemies, like \"and the righteous are bold as a lion\" (Proverbs 28:1)." "<b>To His face.</b> The meaning is: to Himself. And some say it is like \"before Him,\" in His anger, and the meaning is that He repays His enemies because they hated the truth." "<b>To destroy him; He will not delay His enemy.</b> Some say the meaning is: He repays the wicked for the good he did in this world, and He will not delay giving him [punishment] in the World to Come. And the correct view in my eyes is that it stands against His lovers — they stand for a thousand generations; His enemies He destroys. And He added \"He will not delay,\" so that one may think [it applies] to his son or his son's son, like the meaning of \"to the third and fourth [generation]\" (Exodus 34:7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {2 "Resolved abbreviation וי״א as 'and some say'; resolved עוה״ז / עוה״ב as 'this world' / 'the World to Come'; resolved השיב/יאחר ambiguity by translating as printed."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:44.434092119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}